        "id": 19273,
        "name": "Paul",
        "username": "Paul",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/paul/{size}/5862_2.png",
        "created_at": "2019-06-25T21:30:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey everyone!!!</p>\n<p>I wanted to let you all know that, if you are attending Gen Con, you should definitely sign up for the event \"Terror in Megalopolis\". It is a Sentinel Comics LARP co-written by Chrisopher and Adam (who will be there!) and&nbsp;Phoenix Outlaw Productions, who will also be running the event. It is a brand-new system and story and it is going to be *amazing*. We are running 2, each of which has a limit of 35 players. The first will be on Saturday evening at 8pm, and the second will be on Sunday morning at 11am.</p>\n<p>I'm posting about it here not only because it will be amazing and I wanted to make sure all of you know, but also because it wasn't live when Gen Con tickets went on sale, so we have a lot of slots left! I also wanted to explain what \"Terror in Megalopolis\" means, since Gen Con prevented us from using a more logical and useful title like \"Sentinel Comics LARP\".</p>\n<p>Anyhow, if you'll be at Gen Con, definitely sign up! It's worth it!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:53.989Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 6,
        "reads": 4,
        "readers_count": 3,
        "score": 30.8,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 19270,
        "topic_slug": "sentinel-comics-larp-at-gen-con",
